## How to Choose the Right Hotel

Each of the seven Ensana hotels in Marienbad has its own distinct character. This guide will help you find the right fit:

- **Luxury treatment and history** → Ensana Nové Lázně — five-star flagship with Roman Bath
- **Best location by the springs** → Ensana Centrální Lázně — right beside the Colonnade and mineral springs
- **Art Nouveau architecture and elegance** → Ensana Hvězda — Art Nouveau gem with access to the Imperial Spa
- **Families with children** → Ensana Butterfly or Ensana Hvězda — both hotels offer a children's play corner
- **Active holidays and nature** → Ensana Pacifik — gateway to the Slavkov Forest
- **Best value for money** → Ensana Vltava — three-star prices, four-star treatment access
- **Peace and personal service** → Ensana Svoboda — intimate hotel by the forest

## Parking at the Hotels

Arriving by car? Most Ensana hotels offer their own parking — from free unguarded spaces and guarded car parks to underground garages. At the Pacifik, the spaces right by the hotel are for check-in and check-out, with a nearby parking house for the length of your stay. For hotel car parks and garages, **advance reservation is required**, ideally when you book your stay. For the full overview of options, prices and capacity at each hotel — plus information on parking around town — see the [Parking at the Ensana Hotels](/en/parking) page.

## The Ensana Life loyalty programme

Do you return to Mariánské Lázně? The **Ensana Life** loyalty programme is free, never expires, and the discount grows with the nights you stay — up to **20%**, and not just on accommodation but on the spa, wellness and dining too. A classic cure lasts two to three weeks, so a single stay is often enough for the Silver tier. Details, tiers and conditions are on the [Ensana Life](/en/ensana-life) page.

## Booking Tips

- **Book directly at ensanahotels.com** — direct booking often brings perks such as flexible cancellation, room upgrades or complimentary extras.
- **Consider spa packages** — the hotels offer all-inclusive packages covering accommodation, full board, medical examination and a set of treatments. These tend to be significantly better value than booking individually.
- **Plan at least 7 nights** — an effective spa treatment requires at least a week. The ideal length is 14 to 21 nights, particularly for musculoskeletal or respiratory conditions.
- **Take advantage of the off-season** — October to April brings lower rates with equally high-quality treatment. Autumn, with its golden foliage, is particularly enchanting.
- **Peak season** — May to September, especially during the Chopin Festival, hotels fill up quickly. Book well in advance.

## Frequently Asked Questions

### What treatments do Ensana hotels offer?

The Ensana hotels in Marienbad offer a broad spectrum of balneology treatments based on the town's natural healing resources. These include CO₂ baths (carbonated baths with mineral water), peat wraps, mineral baths, inhalation therapy, underwater massage, electrotherapy, magnetic field therapy and physiotherapy. Every stay begins with a medical examination and an individually tailored treatment plan. For a detailed overview, visit the [Springs Overview](/en/springs-overview) page.

### Which hotel is best for families with children?

Ensana Butterfly and Ensana Hvězda are the best choices for families — both offer a dedicated children's play corner. Ensana Butterfly stands out with its modern facilities, indoor pool and accessible rooms, making it a comfortable base for the whole family.

### How long should a spa stay be?

An effective spa treatment requires a minimum of 7 nights. The ideal stay is 14 to 21 nights, especially for chronic musculoskeletal, respiratory or digestive conditions. Many hotels offer preferential rates for longer stays. More about the [best time to visit](/en/best-time-to-visit).

### Are the hotels wheelchair accessible?

Yes, most Ensana hotels have accessible rooms and adapted facilities. Ensana Butterfly (modern building) and Ensana Nové Lázně offer the most accessible rooms. Please inform the hotel of your needs when booking so that your room and treatments can be prepared in advance.

### How do I get to Marienbad?

Mariánské Lázně is easily reached by car, train or bus. The town lies approximately 160 km west of Prague and 60 km south of Karlovy Vary. The nearest international airports are in Prague and Munich. For a detailed transport guide, visit the [Getting There](/en/getting-there) page.
